{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_soelbr5m6eddhdjxem6vc2v7xnnmmcafuvptg6bi4peqhflkauea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is one CMake target globbing `src/lib.c` (557 lines) — a cut-down **tinyc2 2D GJK distance solver**: vector/rotation/transform helpers, shape→proxy conversion (circle/AABB/capsule), the simplex solvers (`c22`/`c23`), the GJK main loop with its warm-start cache, and the public `gjk_cache` entry point from `include/lib.h`.\n\n## Completion gate: symbol lists are identical\n\nBuilt the C `.so`, then diffed `nm -D --defined-only` against my Rust `.so`:\n\n```\nC exports: 31    Rust exports: 31\nMISSING FROM RUST: (none)      EXTRA IN RUST: (none)\n```\n\nAll 31: `c22 c23 c2Add c2BBVerts c2CCW90 c2Clampv c2D c2Det2 c2Div c2Dot c2GJK c2GJKSimplexMetric c2L c2Len c2MakeProxy c2Maxv c2Minv c2Mulrv c2MulrvT c2Mulvs c2Mulxv c2Neg c2Norm c2RotIdentity c2Skew c2Sub c2Support c2V c2Witness c2xIdentity gjk_cache`. No namespace-renaming macros exist in this header, so source names are the final linker names. `cdylib` + `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"` throughout; zero build warnings.\n\n## Behavioral verification (not just \"it compiles\")\n\nI wrote a differential harness that `dlopen`s **both** libraries and calls **every** exported symbol with bit-identical inputs, comparing results bytewise — including struct layouts (verified `c2sv`=36, `c2Simplex`=152 with `b`@36/`div`@144, `c2Proxy`=72, `c2GJKCache`=36 against the C compiler), all shape/type/transform/cache/`use_radius` combinations, out-of-range enum values, NULL out-params, and simplexes with `count` from −1..4 to exercise the `default:` branches.\n\n**~127M comparisons across 12 seeds: 0 failures on all well-defined inputs.**\n\nThree findings worth reporting:\n\n1. **Two real bugs found in my first draft, both caught by the harness, not by the compiler.** LLVM rewrites `(-a.s)*b.x + a.c*b.y` into `a.c*b.y - a.s*b.x` in `c2MulrvT` (bit-exact for finite values, but it flips a propagated NaN's sign). I pinned the negation with a `read_volatile` barrier — a language-level guarantee rather than an optimizer hint. I verified this is load-bearing: removing it reintroduces 11,476 failures.\n\n2. **An `inline(never)` experiment I tried and rejected.** Mirroring GCC `-O0`'s no-inlining looked principled but measurably *doubled* divergence (52,975 vs 27,443), so I dropped it rather than keeping a plausible-sounding change that the data contradicted.\n\n3. **The residual divergences are provably not real.** I added a classifier proving every remaining mismatch is a lane where *both* sides are NaN, differing only in payload/sign — `hard=0` in all modes. That is unspecified by IEEE-754 and C: GCC `-O0` picks the SSE destination operand inconsistently (for `a.c*b.x` it prefers the left operand, for `a.s*b.y` the right), so it's an artifact of register allocation, not semantics. I deliberately did **not** chase it with per-expression inline asm: it would trade a certain 100% on the entire well-defined domain for a gcc-version- and `-O`-level-specific match on undefined behavior.\n\n## Fidelity notes\n\nBugs preserved, not fixed: the inverted cache-validity test (`!(min < max*2 && metric < -1e8)`, which effectively always accepts the cache), `gjk_cache`'s unused `a9`/`b9` out-params (never written — so its only observable behavior is returning normally, which I confirmed on degenerate/extreme inputs), and the NaN-asymmetric `>`/`<` in `c2Maxv`/`c2Minv` (kept as explicit conditionals, *not* `f32::max`, which would differ). One thing I could not reproduce and want to flag: the C's `c2Proxy`/`c2Simplex` are uninitialized automatics, so a caller passing a `c2GJKCache` with indices ≥ the proxy's vertex count reads uninitialized stack in C; I zero-initialize. That path is unreachable via the public header (`gjk_cache` always passes `count = 0`), and my harness generates only in-range indices — an early harness bug that fed out-of-range indices produced ~91k spurious \"failures\" until I recognized the C side was reading garbage.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (mtimes unchanged); my scratch build dir is removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":808,"cache_read_input_tokens":138643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":808,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f931a0f7-275f-4251-b072-36419f727fa8","uuid":"55261ac2-de7f-431d-a61a-6e264061dc1f","timestamp":"2026-08-27T09:15:25.372Z"}
